WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:09.829
Ally was looking around her bedroom one last time when Mateo came in.

2
00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:16.736
"I guess it's time." Ally held back tears. "I'm going home."

3
00:00:16.737 --> 00:00:22.799
"Yep," Mateo said. "Thanks again for giving us Alpha's computer."

4
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.384
"Of course! Alpha has no use for it anymore.

5
00:00:26.385 --> 00:00:30.002
Alpha's chip is stored safely on Tina's ship."

6
00:00:30.003 --> 00:00:33.939
Ally picked up her bag as Mateo's phone pinged.

7
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.260
"It's Papi," he said.

8
00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:39.645
"Can you stop by the diner on your way to the airport?"

9
00:00:39.646 --> 00:00:42.355
"Do you know why?" Ally asked.

10
00:00:42.356 --> 00:00:46.659
"I have to meet Tina. And I've already said good-bye to everyone."

11
00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:53.007
"Maybe he's made his decision about Big City Foods and wants to tell us there," Mateo said.

12
00:00:53.008 --> 00:00:58.707
"I'm sorry I won't be here to help, whatever he decides," Ally replied.

13
00:00:58.708 --> 00:01:02.793
"You've already helped us all so much," Mateo said.

14
00:01:02.794 --> 00:01:05.764
"I wish we had a way to stay in touch."

15
00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:10.715
"I'll ask my parents to find a way for us to communicate," Ally said.

16
00:01:10.716 --> 00:01:13.723
"Do you think they can?" Mateo said.

17
00:01:13.724 --> 00:01:18.259
"They'd better!" Ally threw her arms around Mateo.

18
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:24.035
"Thank you for being my friend, and for making this planet feel like home."

19
00:01:24.036 --> 00:01:33.629
Mateo was teary too. "You'll always have a home here."

20
00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:37.250
At the diner Mateo held open the door.

21
00:01:37.251 --> 00:01:40.429
Inside it was dark and silent.

22
00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:44.148
Ally was confused. "Why are all the lights . . . ?"

23
00:01:44.149 --> 00:01:50.499
The lights snapped on, and shouts of surprise rang out. "Surprise!"

24
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:58.854
Ray, Phil, Kate, Bethany, Randy, and Flo jumped out from behind the counter.

25
00:01:58.855 --> 00:02:06.400
A large sign read "We'll Miss You, Ally!", and all of her favorite foods were laid out on the counter.

26
00:02:06.401 --> 00:02:11.379
"You did all of this for me?" Ally cried. "Wow!"

27
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:16.246
"We couldn't let you leave town without a party," Kate said.

28
00:02:16.247 --> 00:02:19.934
Ally's eyes were teary again.

29
00:02:19.935 --> 00:02:23.327
"Sandville won't be the same without you," Ray said.

30
00:02:23.328 --> 00:02:27.106
"But before we start this party, I have an announcement."

31
00:02:27.107 --> 00:02:30.714
A hush fell over the room.

32
00:02:30.715 --> 00:02:34.724
"Here it comes," Mateo whispered to Ally.

33
00:02:34.725 --> 00:02:37.410
They both crossed their fingers.

34
00:02:37.411 --> 00:02:40.954
"I've turned down Big City Foods' offer," Ray said.

35
00:02:40.955 --> 00:02:43.389
"The diner is home to all of us.

36
00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:48.369
I don't want to change anything or lose what makes it special."

37
00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:52.133
Everyone cheered. "Hooray!"

38
00:02:52.134 --> 00:02:56.469
Ray grinned. "Now let's eat!"

39
00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.960
It was finally time for Ally to leave for the airport.

40
00:02:59.961 --> 00:03:06.153
When she picked up her bag again, there wasn't a dry eye in the diner.

41
00:03:06.154 --> 00:03:12.513
"It's bad enough that Tina just took a new job at another museum," Phil moaned.

42
00:03:12.514 --> 00:03:18.129
"I can't believe I'm losing my favorite server too—all on the same day."

43
00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.930
"Hey! What about me?" Flo teased him.

44
00:03:22.931 --> 00:03:26.831
As everyone laughed, Ally turned and winked at Mateo.

45
00:03:26.832 --> 00:03:35.519
Her best friend on Earth smiled back.

46
00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:43.298
The second Commander Tinakron's spaceship docked, Ally raced onto her family's ship.

47
00:03:43.299 --> 00:03:48.310
"Mom, Dad!" she called. "I'm back!"

48
00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:50.610
Ally's parents ran to greet her.

49
00:03:50.611 --> 00:03:54.431
They waved their arms in the traditional Astralian greeting.

50
00:03:54.432 --> 00:03:58.239
But Ally threw her arms around them instead.

51
00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:02.185
"I've missed you so much!"

52
00:04:02.186 --> 00:04:08.093
"We've missed you so much!" Ally's mother wiped away tears.

53
00:04:08.094 --> 00:04:11.593
"Let us look at you," Ally's father said.

54
00:04:11.594 --> 00:04:16.208
Ally released the hug and twirled around.

55
00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:20.439
"You look well and healthy," her mother said.

56
00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.928
"I have so much to tell you!" Ally said.

57
00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:28.553
"We can't wait to hear everything, dear," her mother said.

58
00:04:28.554 --> 00:04:34.440
"Luckily, we had some spotty transmission with your Alpha a few times while you were gone.

59
00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:41.426
We saw you doing some wonderfully kind and helpful things on Earth."

60
00:04:41.427 --> 00:04:46.699
"And you were using your Astralian abilities!" her father said.

61
00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.196
"We want to hear all the details.

62
00:04:49.197 --> 00:04:55.195
But first, Allyzooba, tell us why you embraced us with your arms."

63
00:04:55.196 --> 00:04:59.325
"It's how humans show they love each other," Ally said.

64
00:04:59.326 --> 00:05:05.655
"I see," Ally's mother said. "It is a lovely ritual."

65
00:05:05.656 --> 00:05:09.033
"Very nice." Her father nodded.

66
00:05:09.034 --> 00:05:12.470
"Perhaps you can show all your friends this evening at your party."

67
00:05:12.471 --> 00:05:15.161
"Party?" Ally said.

68
00:05:15.162 --> 00:05:16.782
Her mother beamed.

69
00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:20.799
"We thought you might want to have a belated birthday party.

70
00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.839
You were planning one right before you left, remember?

71
00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.432
And we know how much you love parties."

72
00:05:27.433 --> 00:05:29.064
Ally was startled.

73
00:05:29.065 --> 00:05:36.659
That Allyzooba, the one who'd planned parties and loved shopping and wasn't ready for solo missions, seemed far away now.

74
00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.566
"Almost as distant as planet Earth," she thought.

75
00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:43.319
She shook her head and smiled.

76
00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.579
"Thanks, but no party for me tonight.

77
00:05:46.580 --> 00:06:01.841
All I want to do is stay right here, at home."

